[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4144017219","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117904#issuecomment-4144017219","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117904","id":4144017219,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc73AK9D","user":{"login":"HolonProduction","id":99511741,"node_id":"U_kgDOBe5tvQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/99511741?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction","html_url":"https://github.com/HolonProduction","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-27T17:03:52Z","updated_at":"2026-03-27T17:03:52Z","body":"So I have no clue about C++ move semantics. But shouldn't it be `GDScriptLambdaCallable(..., std::move(captures))` instead of moving in the constructor :thinking:","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4144017219/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4144617670","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117904#issuecomment-4144617670","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117904","id":4144617670,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc73CdjG","user":{"login":"DeeJayLSP","id":60024671,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwMDI0Njcx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/60024671?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP","html_url":"https://github.com/DeeJayLSP","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-27T18:58:27Z","updated_at":"2026-03-27T19:00:15Z","body":"> So I have no clue about C++ move semantics. But shouldn't it be `GDScriptLambdaCallable(..., std::move(captures))` instead of moving in the constructor 🤔\r\n\r\nWe still need to call `std::move()` within the constructor for it to be a move operation (at least that's what IntelliSense reports).\r\n\r\nAlthough the big problem is that the vector in the constructor is `const`, which causes the code to fall back to a copy no matter how many moves we use.\r\n\r\nI'll do a few changes and profile again.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4144617670/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4144738226","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117904#issuecomment-4144738226","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117904","id":4144738226,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc73C6-y","user":{"login":"DeeJayLSP","id":60024671,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwMDI0Njcx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/60024671?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP","html_url":"https://github.com/DeeJayLSP","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-27T19:20:53Z","updated_at":"2026-03-27T19:40:41Z","body":"Turns out I had swapped a bottleneck with a slightly lighter bottleneck. Vectors should be correctly moved now.\r\n\r\nAnd since `GDScriptLambda(Self)Callable`s aren't constructed outside of the GDScript VM, I think it's safe to require the provided vector to be moved.\r\n\r\nProfiler results in main description updated.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4144738226/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4146179118","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117904#issuecomment-4146179118","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117904","id":4146179118,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc73Iawu","user":{"login":"Spartan322","id":4315446,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQzMTU0NDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4315446?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Spartan322","html_url":"https://github.com/Spartan322","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Spartan322/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Spartan322/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Spartan322/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Spartan322/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Spartan322/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Spartan322/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Spartan322/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Spartan322/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Spartan322/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-28T00:48:20Z","updated_at":"2026-03-28T00:48:41Z","body":"rvalue reference parameters need to use `std::move` to perform a move operation, else the variable will promote to an lvalue and you'll end up getting a copy from the variable instead of a move. This is because rvalue reference variables are implicitly treated as lvalues without the `std::move` because the rvalue reference identifier can only be used as an lvalue expression. See [lvalue category on cppreference.com](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/language/value_category.html#lvalue)","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4146179118/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4158744414","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117904#issuecomment-4158744414","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117904","id":4158744414,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc734Wde","user":{"login":"DeeJayLSP","id":60024671,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwMDI0Njcx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/60024671?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP","html_url":"https://github.com/DeeJayLSP","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-30T23:18:19Z","updated_at":"2026-03-31T22:22:07Z","body":"~~Reverting back to the previous version (`std::move` only inside the constructor, but without `const`) because:~~\r\n1. ~~The move operator works just fine like this.~~\r\n2. ~~There are other instances of `std::move`ing inside constructors like this in Godot's codebase.~~\r\n3. ~~We're definitely not constructing `GDScriptLambda(Self)Callable`s outside the GDScript VM, therefore no need to enforce the usage of `std::move` when calling it.~~\r\n\r\n~~If requested, though, I may unrevert.~~ **Edit:** it has been unreverted.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4158744414/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4165900748","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117904#issuecomment-4165900748","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117904","id":4165900748,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc74TpnM","user":{"login":"Shadows-of-Fire","id":3682588,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2ODI1ODg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3682588?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadows-of-Fire","html_url":"https://github.com/Shadows-of-Fire","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadows-of-Fire/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadows-of-Fire/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadows-of-Fire/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadows-of-Fire/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadows-of-Fire/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadows-of-Fire/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadows-of-Fire/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadows-of-Fire/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadows-of-Fire/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-31T22:13:06Z","updated_at":"2026-03-31T22:13:06Z","body":"> There are other instances of std::moveing inside constructors like this in Godot's codebase.\r\n\r\nOther instances of poor behavior is not an excuse to introduce more poor behavior.\r\n\r\n> We're definitely not constructing GDScriptLambda(Self)Callables outside the GDScript VM, therefore no need to enforce the usage of std::move when calling it.\r\n\r\nThat's not really relevant. While we can control for that, it means our static analysis tools will be unable to assist in catching behavioral errors that are trivial to assess when the `std::move` is lifted to the call site. We want to ensure that [`bugprone-use-after-move`](https://clang.llvm.org/extra/clang-tidy/checks/bugprone/use-after-move.html) can detect this class of issues by not obscuring where a move happens.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4165900748/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4173965583","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117904#issuecomment-4173965583","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117904","id":4173965583,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc74yakP","user":{"login":"DeeJayLSP","id":60024671,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwMDI0Njcx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/60024671?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP","html_url":"https://github.com/DeeJayLSP","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-02T01:15:03Z","updated_at":"2026-04-03T02:21:09Z","body":"In case it's relevant, this is the profiling result for [Godot Benchmarks]